summary:
- topic: FY25 Budget Overview
  text: Superintendent Angela Atkinson Duina presented an overview of the Superintendent’sFY25Budget,
    proposing a 5% operating budget increase. She highlighted major constraints, including
    rising fixed costs from collective bargaining agreements and the impending loss
    of $1.5 million in federal COVID-19 relief funds, which currently supports 19
    positions.
- topic: Budget Adjustments
  text: The administration announced a budget-neutral change, moving a high school
    art position previously funded by COVID-era grants into the local budget. To offset
    this, a one-year-only teaching position at Dyer School will be funded from an
    elementary school reserve account.
- topic: Extended Learning Opportunities (ELO) Program
  text: A significant discussion occurred regarding the ELO program, whose coordinator
    position was funded by an expiring state grant. The Superintendent acknowledged
    a 'bumpy' transition but assured the board and public that the popular program
    will continue with a robust model, promising more details on the new staffing
    structure later in the week.
- topic: Departmental Budget Presentations
  text: Directors from five key departments presented their budgets and priorities.
    Special Education detailed student demographics and service models. Adult Education
    highlighted its exponential growth and reliance on unstable grant funding. The
    Technology Department focused on infrastructure upgrades, cybersecurity, and a
    new district app. The Athletics department reviewed program successes and support
    systems. The Operations & Safety department discussed right-sizing budgets for
    transportation, facilities, and food service to reflect actual costs.
- topic: Elementary School Reconfiguration Postponement
  text: The Superintendent announced that the workshop on ElementaryBoundariesandConfigurations,
    originally scheduled for this meeting, was postponed to the April 8th regular
    board meeting to ensure broader public participation following recent power outages.
- topic: Board and Public Comment
  text: Board members expressed strong support for the ELO and art programs, with
    several advocating for a dedicated grant writer position to secure future funding.
    Public commenters shared powerful testimonials on the positive impact of both
    the Special Education and ELO programs, urging the board to ensure their continued
    support.
